tory\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Dinwiddie County came in under 90% of normal in September to October 37 times in 75 years since 1951, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle ran 154% of normal in June to July and only 46% in October to November. So far in 2026 the middle got 38% of normal in March to April. July to August is the wettest pair at 9.28 inches normal, and October to November is the driest at 6.60.</p>"}
